<https://mesh.kib.ki.se/>
    dcterms:title "Svensk MeSH 2026 (Swedish translation of Medical Subject Headings)" ;
    dcterms:creator "Karolinska Institutets Universitetsbibliotek (Swedish translation); U.S. National Library of Medicine (MeSH)" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    rdfs:comment "https://mesh.kib.ki.se/info/om-webbplatsen (fetched 2026-10-25) — \"Licensen som tillhandahålls av KIB är också gratis och berättigar till att använda en kopia av de tabeller som gränssnittet är baserat på. Data distribueras under CC0. Ange Karolinska Institutets Bibliotek som upphovsman.\" The same page continues: \"Själva MeSH-vokabulären produceras av NLM (the National Library of Medicine). All användning av MeSH® är föremål för de restriktioner som anges i NLM:s villkor för användning av MeSH\". Content: Swedish front names (preferred terms and synonyms) and facts in the Swedish scope notes."@en .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/>
    dcterms:title "Medical Subject Headings (MeSH), RDF and lookup services" ;
    dcterms:creator "U.S. National Library of Medicine" ;
    rdfs:comment "https://www.nlm.nih.gov/databases/download/terms_and_conditions_mesh.html (fetched 2026-10-25) — \"NLM freely provides MeSH data.\" Users agree to \"acknowledge NLM as the source of the data in a clear and conspicuous manner, not indicate or imply that NLM has endorsed its products/services/applications.\" https://www.nlm.nih.gov/web_policies.html (fetched 2026-10-25) — \"Works produced by the U.S. government are not subject to copyright protection in the United States. Any such works found on National Library of Medicine (NLM) Web sites may be freely used or reproduced without permission in the U.S.\" Content: facts on location and function from the English scope notes and descriptor trees; NLM is credited as their source and nothing implies its endorsement."@en .

<https://www.ninds.nih.gov/health-information/public-education/brain-basics/brain-basics-know-your-brain>
    dcterms:title "Brain Basics: Know Your Brain" ;
    dcterms:creator "National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke (NINDS), U.S. National Institutes of Health" ;
    rdfs:comment "A fact sheet on an official website of the United States government (the page's banner: \"An official website of the United States government\"); as a work of the U.S. federal government it is not subject to copyright in the United States (17 U.S.C. § 105). The page shows no license statement of its own. Fetched once, on 2026-10-25, with the project's own User-Agent and as its robots.txt allows; later requests were refused, and nothing was fetched from it after that. Content: facts on the lobes, motor and sensory areas, the hippocampus and the basal ganglia; no wording was taken."@en .

